The client another box speaks to this box's /api/v1 with, kept here word for
word so that check-remotebox.sh drives the code a peer really runs and not a
reading of it.

Files under system/ are taken as they stand from the peer's tree, paths
src/system/remotetimer.{h,cpp} and src/system/httptool.{h,cpp}. Which tree
state: the one the importing commit's provenance note names (upstream
73789a23608de410542a514510912adff6879663, the same tree as mirror commit
73048d540497); the Origin block of that commit names the commit that first
introduced the client, which is a different thing. The files are never
edited: a refresh is a checkout of those paths at the new tree state, recorded
in the commit message the same way. Anything this tree needs that the peer's
files do not offer goes into remotebox_client.cpp beside them.

The directory is put first on the include path of that one program, so the
client's own <system/httptool.h> is the one it was written against; the tree's
own httptool is not part of this program.
